    <!-- Micro-Period Titles, Bodies & Hormones -->
    <string name="cycle_menstrual_early_title">Menstrual Release &amp; Rest</string>
    <string name="cycle_menstrual_early_body">Uterine prostaglandins peak, signaling natural shedding. Energy is at resting baseline. Prioritize warmth, iron replenishment, and gentle pacing.</string>
    <string name="cycle_menstrual_early_hormones">Estrogen and progesterone are at baseline low. Prostaglandin activity is high.</string>

    <string name="cycle_menstrual_late_title">Renewal &amp; Energy Awakening</string>
    <string name="cycle_menstrual_late_body">Bleeding subsides and the uterine lining begins rebuilding. Cellular repair is active. Your body naturally sheds cycle fluid.</string>
    <string name="cycle_menstrual_late_hormones">Estrogen begins its gradual, steady ascent. Progesterone remains quiet.</string>

    <string name="cycle_follicular_early_title">Rising Power &amp; Mental Sharpness</string>
    <string name="cycle_follicular_early_body">Insulin sensitivity is peak: muscles absorb carbs effortlessly as clean fuel. Serotonin and motivation climb rapidly.</string>
    <string name="cycle_follicular_early_hormones">Rising estradiol stimulates follicular development and neurochemical vitality.</string>

    <string name="cycle_follicular_late_title">Pre-Ovulatory Radiance</string>
    <string name="cycle_follicular_late_body">Stamina, metabolic flexibility, and physical strength are at their cycle highs. A small testosterone surge amplifies confidence.</string>
    <string name="cycle_follicular_late_hormones">Estrogen peaks; mild testosterone surge occurs before the ovulatory trigger.</string>

    <string name="cycle_ovulation_title">Ovulatory Peak &amp; Vitality</string>
    <string name="cycle_ovulation_body">The LH surge triggers egg release; basal body temperature rises by ~0.3°C. Social energy and metabolic turnover are at their zenith.</string>
    <string name="cycle_ovulation_hormones">LH surge, peak estrogen, and the transition into progesterone synthesis.</string>

    <string name="cycle_luteal_early_title">Metabolic Acceleration</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_early_body">Progesterone takes the lead, boosting your basal metabolic rate by +100 to 200 kcal/day. Moderate appetite increase is biologically necessary.</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_early_hormones">Progesterone dominates, activating GABA calming pathways while body temperature stays elevated.</string>

    <string name="cycle_luteal_mid_title">Progesterone Peak &amp; Fluid Shift</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_mid_body">Aldosterone activates renal sodium retention: 0.8–1.5 kg scale weight increase is common fluid holding, NOT body fat! Magnesium soothes irritability.</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_mid_hormones">Peak progesterone; aldosterone elevated; mild drop in insulin sensitivity.</string>

    <string name="cycle_luteal_late_title">PMS Threshold &amp; Fluid Peak</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_late_body">Hormone withdrawal can trigger fluid retention up to 2.5 kg and serotonin dips. Do not let the scale trick you. Rest, hydrate, and steer clear of excess salt.</string>
    <string name="cycle_luteal_late_hormones">Rapid drop in estrogen and progesterone prior to menstruation.</string>

